codemap 8
path map-file
kind type
author ai
group map
note The map itself: the only thing this tool persists. A directory, .codemap, at the root, committed with the code, with one text file per path holding its kind, group, note, author and steps. The format is hand-rolled, one field per line, no serialization dependency and no JSON. It exists to merge: two branches that change different paths touch different files, and two that change one path touch different lines unless they edit the same field of the same step. A file written by another version is refused outright and the map regenerated. The model (Map, Path, Step) lives in domain and knows nothing of files; the io-map crate is the boundary: wire.rs is the text layout (CmapPath and CmapStep, parse, render), convert.rs turns it into domain values and back, and MapStore in lib.rs reads and writes the directory. Every read fault is data (ParseError, MapLoadError, MapSaveError) that cli's wire.rs words.

